---
const elsewhere = [
  { label: 'GitHub', href: 'https://github.com/rizkhal', handle: 'rizkhal' },
  { label: 'X', href: 'https://x.com/rixzkl', handle: '@rixzkl' },
]
---

<section id="about" class="wrap py-20 md:py-28">
  <div class="grid gap-14 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-10">
    <div class="lg:col-span-7">
      <h2 class="display text-[clamp(2rem,4.4vw,3.4rem)]">About</h2>

      <p class="display mt-8 max-w-[24ch] text-[clamp(1.4rem,2.6vw,2rem)] leading-[1.15] text-paper">
        The interesting part is rarely the model.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-7 max-w-[62ch] space-y-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-mist md:text-base">
        <p>
          I work at Lamaau Labs in Jakarta, mostly on internal tools that turn awkward public data
          into something a person can actually use. Legal corpora, fisheries statistics, vessel
          positions, satellite tiles. It is the ingest, the cache, and the one field that arrives as
          a string on Tuesdays.
        </p>
        <p>
          Everything I build runs on infrastructure I can read end to end: Postgres, SQLite, Hono,
          Docker, one VPS, and a reverse proxy. I would rather ship a boring system that survives
          contact with real data than a clever one that needs a babysitter.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="lg:col-span-5 lg:pl-10">
      <h3 class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-ochre/75">Elsewhere</h3>
      <ul class="mt-4 grid gap-px bg-ochre/12">
        {
          elsewhere.map((item) => (
            <li class="bg-ink/60">
              <a
                href={item.href}
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener me"
                class="group flex items-center justify-between gap-4 px-1 py-4"
              >
                <span class="text-sm text-paper transition-colors duration-300 group-hover:text-sun">
                  {item.label}
                </span>
                <span class="font-mono text-[11px] text-ochre/75">{item.handle}</span>
              </a>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
